    {
      "title": "Mumbai Police ask actor Imran Khan, a US national, to leave India by Oct 28",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/mumbai-police-ask-actor-imran-khan-a-us-national-to-leave-india-by-oct-28-126101500338_1.html",
      "description": "The Mumbai Police have issued a notice to Bollywood actor Imran Khan, an American national, directing him to leave India by October 28 for allegedly violating provisions of the Immigration and Foreigners Act, officials said on Thursday.\nThe action comes after the actor, nephew of superstar Aamir Khan, participated in an agitation on October 10 in Mumbai, where protesters demanded the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar, the police official said.\nDuring the demonstration, the police had also briefly taken the actor into custody.\n\"Imran Khan holds foreign citizenship and is not an Indian national. Under relevant provisions of the Foreigners/Immigration Act, foreign nationals are prohibited from participating in political protests or political activities on Indian soil,\" a police official said.\nA formal notice directing the actor to leave the country by October 28 has been served on him, and he has received a copy, the police said. Further administrative procedure",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-15T05:58:09"
    }
